  "result": "The gate passes NRS_484B_270_2b_o3 (**OK**, 9 witnesses). It passed on the first run and again after I changed only the header comment, so 2 of the 6 runs are used.\n\nThe one thing to look at: **the five \"unless\" compositions in b11 are not in the rule.** The gate accepted this but reports \"composes nothing\". They point at b12, which the node carries only as a residue: the permission to pass left of center or in a no-passing zone relaxes NRS 484B.213 and 217, and leaves this rule's duty unchanged. Because b12 has no formula here, there is nothing to attach the compositions to, and putting them anywhere else would change when the rule applies. The planner may want to remove them or point them elsewhere.\n\n**What the rule says:**\n- **When it applies:** the subject is a motor vehicle overtaking some other road user r that is:\n  - a bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;\n  - moving in the same direction as the subject;\n  - seen ahead of the subject at some point in the overtaking window, and now either not yet behind it or already passed;\n  - on the subject's right;\n  - in a lane that is the only one in its direction.\n- **The duty:** until the subject is safely clear, its heading may not turn right of any lane r occupies. Safely clear means r is behind the subject with a gap of at least r's speed times the following headway. The headway is the ice value on ice or snow, otherwise the wet value on a wet road or in rain, otherwise the dry value.\n\n**Choices the node left open:**\n- **\"The pass has been recognised\":** the pass concept is true only at the moment it is recognised, so I wrote this as \"it was true at some moment in the window\".\n- **The literal \"one\" lane:** the units have no count constructor, so I wrote it as `Units.ratio 1 1` with the count unit; the gate accepted it.\n- **Narrowings:** none of my own.\n\n**Witnesses:** besides the six planned scenarios, I added three more where the subject steers back right at a gap that would be clear on a dry road but not on a wet road (branch_3), in rain (branch_4) or on ice (branch_5). All three expect violated, and they check that the headway switches correctly.\n\nTwo commands I tried early on were blocked because only the gate command may run here. One was a directory listing, the other a gate call with an extra `--help` flag. Neither affected the result.\n\nFiles are in `library/` and in the iter-007 results folder for this node:\n- library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_270_2b_o3.lean\n- library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_270_2b_o3.lean\n- task_result.md",
